# Reinstall API after code change

When this agent changes **alamut-api** (sibling repo), it must reinstall the Windows service — remove the old version and install the new build — before saying the change is live.

## Script (in alamut-api)

```powershell
# From C:\Users\armin\GitHub\alamut-api; requires Administrator
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\scripts\reinstall-windows-service.ps1
```

## When to run

1. Any turn that edited alamut-api code that ships in the service binary
2. Same conditions as `alamut-api/.cursor/rules/reinstall-after-code-change.mdc`

## When not to run

1. **alamut-webui**-only edits (cold rebuild/run WebUI per `rebuild-edited-section-only.mdc`; do not reinstall API)
2. Docs-only or comment-only API edits
3. Script already succeeded this turn for the same change

## Note

WebUI changes do **not** use this script. Only API binary / service updates do.
